enjoys uninterrupted sea and garden views while offering residents access to Gymnasium, Swimming Pool, Power Backup, Treated Water Supply, 24 x 7 Security, CCTV / Video Surveillance, Party Hall, Clubhouse, Rain Water Harvesting, Sewage Treatment Plant, including the exclusive Club Saint Amand and personalised hospitality services. The project is registered under RERA No. P51900034949, P51900055626.\n\nPositioned on the iconic Walkeshwar Road, Lodha Malabar introduces a limited collection of ultra-luxury residences overlooking both the Arabian Sea and the Hanging Gardens. Inspired by Mumbai's celebrated Art Deco heritage, the development combines timeless architecture with expansive sea-facing homes, curated hospitality, and one of South Mumbai's most distinguished residential addresses. Located at Malabar Hill Mumbai, the development enjoys uninterrupted sea and garden views while offering residents access to Gymnasium, Swimming Pool, Power Backup, Treated Water Supply, 24 x 7 Security, CCTV / Video Surveillance, Party Hall, Clubhouse, Rain Water Harvesting, Sewage Treatment Plant, including the exclusive Club Saint Amand and personalised hospitality services. The project is registered under RERA No. P51900034949, P51900055626.\n\n![Lodha Malabar Cover Image](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/project-image/lodha-malabar-project-project-large-image1-3945.jpg?aio=w-725;h-350;crop;)\n![Lodha Malabar Amenities-Features](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/project-image/lodha-malabar-project-amenities-features1-4819.jpg?aio=w-192;h-168;crop;)\n![Lodha Malabar Amenities-Features](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/project-image/lodha-malabar-project-amenities-features4-6188.jpg?aio=w-192;h-168;crop;)\n![Lodha Malabar Video](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/tn-projectflagship/tn-lodha-malabar-project-flagship.jpg?aio=w-192;h-168;crop;)\n\n**Price on Request**\n\n## Why you should consider Lodha Malabar?\n\n## About Lodha Malabar, Malabar Hill by Lodha\n\nCertain addresses become landmarks because of their location, while a select few earn recognition through the experience they create. Lodha Malabar belongs to the latter category. Rising on one of the largest land parcels in Malabar Hill, the development has been conceived as an Art Deco-inspired residential landmark that celebrates South Mumbai's architectural legacy while introducing contemporary luxury living. Situated at Malabar Hill Mumbai, opposite the Governor's Estate and overlooking both the Arabian Sea and the Hanging Gardens, the project offers a setting that is rarely available in Mumbai's luxury residential market. Every residence has been planned to capture panoramic views of the sea and surrounding greenery, allowing the location itself to become an integral part of everyday living.\n\nThe architectural language pays tribute to Mumbai's historic Art Deco movement through elegant proportions, intricate detailing, and enduring craftsmanship. Complementing the residences is Club Saint Amand, an exclusive private members' club designed around wellness, leisure, hospitality, and social experiences. Residents also benefit from personalized services delivered by Lodha's in-house hospitality team, bringing the attentiveness of a luxury hotel into a private residential setting. The project is registered under RERA No. P51900034949, P51900055626, further reinforcing transparency for prospective homebuyers.\n\n### Key USPs of Lodha Malabar\n\nLodha Malabar has been envisioned as more than a premium residential tower. It combines heritage-inspired architecture, an irreplaceable location, curated hospitality, and limited-edition residences to create one of South Mumbai's most exclusive addresses.\n\n#### 1. Landmark Address in Malabar Hill\n\nLocated on Walkeshwar Road, opposite the Governor's Estate and overlooking both the Arabian Sea and the Hanging Gardens, the project occupies one of South Mumbai's most prestigious residential locations.\n\n#### 2. Contemporary Interpretation of Art Deco Architecture\n\nThe development draws inspiration from Mumbai's iconic Art Deco heritage, incorporating refined geometry, intricate detailing, and premium craftsmanship to create an architectural identity that is both timeless and contemporary.\n\n#### 3. Club Saint Amand\n\nResidents enjoy access to Club Saint Amand, an exclusive private members' club planned around wellness, recreation, leisure, and social experiences, creating a lifestyle beyond the residence itself.\n\n#### 4. Luxury Hospitality Services\n\nDedicated hospitality professionals provide personalized residential services inspired by five-star hotels, delivering a seamless living experience with discreet and attentive service.\n\n#### 5. Limited Collection of Sea-Facing Residences\n\nSet on one of the largest land parcels in Malabar Hill, Lodha Malabar offers expansive residences with uninterrupted views of the Arabian Sea and surrounding greenery, creating a level of exclusivity that is increasingly rare in South Mumbai\n\nCertain addresses become landmarks because of their location, while a select few earn recognition through the experience they create. Lodha Malabar belongs to the latter category. Rising on one of the largest land parcels in Malabar Hill, the development has been conceived as an Art Deco-inspired residential landmark that celebrates South Mumbai's architectural legacy while introducing contemporary luxury living. Situated at Malabar Hill Mumbai, opposite the Governor's Estate and overlooking both the Arabian Sea and the Hanging Gardens, the project offers a setting that is rarely available in Mumbai's luxury residential market. Every residence has been planned to capture panoramic views of the sea and surrounding greenery, allowing the location itself to become an integral part of everyday living.\n\nThe architectural language pays tribute to Mumbai's historic Art Deco movement through el